  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given rectangle \\(R_1\\) with one side \\(2\\) inches and area \\(12\\) square inches. Rectangle \\(R_2\\) with diagonal \\(15\\) inches is similar to \\(R_1.\\) Expressed in square inches the area of \\(R_2\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac92\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(36\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{135}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(9\\sqrt{10}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{27\\sqrt{10}}4\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "135/2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The diagonal of \\(R_1\\) is \\(\\sqrt{2^2+6^2}=2\\sqrt{10}.\\) Therefore \\[ \\frac{[R_2]}{[R_1]} =\\left(\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{10}}\\right)^2 =\\frac{45}{8}. \\] Thus \\([R_2]=12(\\frac{45}{8})=\\frac{135}{2}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "The sides of \\(R_1\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(6\\)",
        "Areas scale as the square of the ratio of corresponding diagonals"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
